  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 109,
    "summary": "David speaks of the cursings due to the wicked and deceitful—He prays that his enemies will be confounded.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Hold not thy peace, O God of my praise;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:1",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "For the mouth of the wicked and the mouth of the deceitful are opened against me: they have spoken against me with a lying tongue.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 117,
            "end": 122,
            "text": "D&C 109:30 (29–30)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:2",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "They compassed me about also with words of hatred; and fought against me without a cause.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:3",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "For my love they are my adversaries: but I give myself unto prayer.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3,
            "text": "JST Ps. 109:4 And, notwithstanding my love, they are my adversaries; yet I will continue in prayer for them."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:4",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And they have rewarded me evil for good, and hatred for my love.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "1 Jn. 3:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Jn. 3:15.",
            "prettyString": "1 John 3:15",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1john",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 3,
                    "end": 3,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 15,
                        "end": 15
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:5",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Set thou a wicked man over him: and let Satan stand at his right hand.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "HEB an adversary, accuser. Zech. 3:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:6",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "When he shall be judged, let him be condemned: and let his prayer become sin.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "James 2:13; Hel. 8:25; D&C 10:23 (20–23); 121:24 (23–25)."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "Prov. 28:9; Mosiah 11:25 (24–25)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:7",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Let his days be few; and let another take his office.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "Acts 1:20 (16–20)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 24
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:8",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Let his children be fatherless, and his wife a widow.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:9",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Let his children be continually vagabonds, and beg: let them seek their bread also out of their desolate places.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 77
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:10",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Let the extortioner catch all that he hath; and let the strangers spoil his labour.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "OR creditors seize."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:11",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Let there be none to extend mercy unto him: neither let there be any to favour his fatherless children.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:12",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Let his posterity be cut off; and in the generation following let their name be blotted out.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "Ps. 21:10 (10–11); 37:28; Isa. 14:20; 2 Ne. 24:20; D&C 121:15 (13–15)."
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "Mosiah 26:36; Alma 5:57 (56–58); D&C 20:83."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 33
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:13",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Let the iniquity of his fathers be remembered with the Lord; and let not the sin of his mother be blotted out.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "Ex. 20:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ex. 20:5.",
            "prettyString": "Exodus 20:5",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "exodus",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 20,
                    "end": 20,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 5,
                        "end": 5
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:14",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Let them be before the Lord continually, that he may cut off the memory of them from the earth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:15",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Because that he remembered not to shew mercy, but persecuted the poor and needy man, that he might even slay the broken in heart.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "Ps. 86:1; Alma 5:55 (54–56); Hel. 6:39 (39–40); D&C 56:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:16",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "As he loved cursing, so let it come unto him: as he delighted not in blessing, so let it be far from him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:17",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "As he clothed himself with cursing like as with his garment, so let it come into his bowels like water, and like oil into his bones.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:18",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Let it be unto him as the garment which covereth him, and for a girdle wherewith he is girded continually.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 39
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:19",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Let this be the reward of mine adversaries from the Lord, and of them that speak evil against my soul.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 11
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:20",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "But do thou for me, O God the Lord, for thy name’s sake: because thy mercy is good, deliver thou me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "Ps. 23:3; 25:11; 31:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 77
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ps. 23:3; 25:11; 31:3.",
            "prettyString": "Psalms 23:3; 25:11; 31:3",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "psalms",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 23,
                    "end": 23,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 3,
                        "end": 3
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "start": 25,
                    "end": 25,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 11,
                        "end": 11
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "start": 31,
                    "end": 31,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 3,
                        "end": 3
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:21",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "For I am poor and needy, and my heart is wounded within me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 8
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:22",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "I am gone like the shadow when it declineth: I am tossed up and down as the locust.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:23",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "My knees are weak through fasting; and my flesh faileth of fatness.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:24",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "I became also a reproach unto them: when they looked upon me they shaked their heads.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:25",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "Help me, O Lord my God: O save me according to thy mercy:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:26",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "That they may know that this is thy hand; that thou, Lord, hast done it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 31
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 46
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:27",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "Let them curse, but bless thou: when they arise, let them be ashamed; but let thy servant rejoice.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG Curse."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Curse.",
            "prettyString": "TG Curse",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Curse",
                "entryId": "tg-curse",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:28",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "Let mine adversaries be clothed with shame, and let them cover themselves with their own confusion, as with a mantle.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "Ps. 71:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ps. 71:13.",
            "prettyString": "Psalms 71:13",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "psalms",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 71,
                    "end": 71,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 13,
                        "end": 13
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:29",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "I will greatly praise the Lord with my mouth; yea, I will praise him among the multitude.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 109:30",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 109,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "For he shall stand at the right hand of the poor, to save him from those that condemn his soul.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "Ps. 16:8."
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "D&C 56:18 (15–18)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
